[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539000138","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112841#issuecomment-3539000138","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112841","id":3539000138,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S8NtK","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T17:32:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T17:35:32Z","body":"This is because your character's shoulders are inverted from the rest pose in animation. See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106623.\n\nIn the rest, shoulder +Z is back:\n<img width=\"510\" height=\"421\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/71587882-0a41-497e-9518-e12a8bccb1d7\" />\n\nBut animation, shoulder +Z is front:\n<img width=\"408\" height=\"416\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17eacb83-0dfd-4c7b-8e61-9c95d7e5ae50\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539000138/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539928365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112841#issuecomment-3539928365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112841","id":3539928365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S_wUt","user":{"login":"aromancev","id":29806368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODA2MzY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29806368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev","html_url":"https://github.com/aromancev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T04:42:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T04:43:44Z","body":"Thank you for taking a look @TokageItLab!\n\nThe problem is, this animation is created in Blender using inverse kinematics where I don't really control how the bone is rotated. I guess I could try adding rotation constraints to the shoulder. Would you say it's the correct way to go about it?\n\nThanks again for your advice and a detailed explanation ♥️ ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539928365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3540010253","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112841#issuecomment-3540010253","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112841","id":3540010253,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TAEUN","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T05:09:59Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T05:14:16Z","body":"> I guess I could try adding rotation constraints to the shoulder. Would you say it's the correct way to go about it?\n\nIt possibly works if you import all animations as IK animations, but it is not recommended as long as you use FK.\n\nAs mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106623#issuecomment-2893190797, animations facing the opposite direction of the rest pose will actually import as animations facing the opposite direction. Generally, with skinned models, rotations exceeding 180 degrees can result in skin collapse or bone fractures and penetrating the body. Therefore, animation blending attempts to avoid rotations exceeding 180 degrees, see also https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/animation/animation_tree.html#for-better-blending.\n\nThe first recommended step is to make each bone's rest pose distinguishable on the model (by coloring one face or adding marker objects) and ensure that the twist in each animation does not exceed 180 degrees from the rest pose. \n\nRest pose means edit mode bone state in Blender, you can check the axes with Viewport Display setting or Normal Mode Gizmo.\n\n<img width=\"1096\" height=\"449\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ff9104d0-4e2c-40b4-a48f-bdfef9aec807\" />\n\n<img width=\"559\" height=\"611\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4329907f-b540-44ed-a25d-a8abf903a5e0\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3540010253/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3540053357","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112841#issuecomment-3540053357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112841","id":3540053357,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TAO1t","user":{"login":"aromancev","id":29806368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODA2MzY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29806368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev","html_url":"https://github.com/aromancev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T05:32:10Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T05:32:10Z","body":"Clear, thank you very much! \n\nSo basically, no animation should rotate any bone by 180 degrees or more from the rest pose. If it does, it breaks blending because blending is done via the rest pose instead of via the shortest route to avoid bones passing through the body.\n\nI will try to limit bone rotation with constraints for the IK skeleton. I think it will also work with FK because I have separate skeletons for IK and FK that drive the deform skeleton. So IK constraints won't get in the way when I animate FK.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3540053357/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]